# Oracle guard for #1423: YAML 1.1 requires a '.' in the plain-float form, so PyYAML types
# "1e-7" as the STRING '1e-7'; Sharpy's YamlScalarResolver is more permissive and returns the
# float 1e-07. This fixture pins Sharpy's CURRENT (divergent) behavior so the differential
# oracle guards the divergence live — its allowlist entry cites #1423 and drains when it lands,
# at which point the expected output becomes "1e-7" / 4 (the string, unchanged by load).
#
# The LENGTH line is what makes the divergence oracle-visible at all: printed bare, the two
# arms show `1e-07` vs `1e-7`, which the oracle's float-tolerant OutputComparer deliberately
# treats as equal formatting of the same number. A type divergence that prints as an equal
# number is invisible to a stdout oracle — the string's length is not.
import yaml

def main():
    v = yaml.safe_load("1e-7")
    print(v)
    print(len(str(v)))
